<title>CANADA: CWB details Prairie elevator space, railcar unload.</title>
<headline>CWB details Prairie elevator space, railcar unload.</headline>
<dateline>WINNIPEG 1997-07-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>Vacant space in Canadian Prairie primary grain elevators remained steady at 22 percent in the week ended July 27, Canadian Wheat Board said.</p>
<p>Manitoba elevators had the most free space at 28 percent, Alberta was next at 26 percent followed by Saskatchewan at 18 percent.</p>
<p>Vancouver unloaded 2,932 railcars versus the 3,300 target. Prince Rupert unloaded 1,227 railcars versus the 900 target. Thunder Bay unloaded 3,723 railcars versus the 3,550 target.</p>
<p>((Gilbert Le Gras, Winnipeg Reuters bureau 204 947 3548))</p>
